      "text": "**Ama Owusu** is a debut novelist who has an MFA from the University of East Anglia. Her short fiction has been featured in notable publications such as *Granta*, *Jalada Africa*, and *Transition*. She is based in Accra, and *Glassy-eyed* is her first novel, with hints that a second novel is in progress. \n\n*Glassy-eyed*, published in January 2023 by Cassava Press, is a multigenerational novel set in contemporary Accra, following three generations of a family through a glass-blower's workshop. The book consists of 287 pages and bears the ISBN 978-1-73625-441-8. The first printing of 3,000 copies quickly sold out by March 2023, leading to a second printing in April 2023. The novel has received critical acclaim, being longlisted for the Etisalat Prize for Literature (2023) and shortlisted for the Commonwealth Writers Prize (Africa region) in 2024.\n\nFor further details, you can refer to:\n- [Ama Owusu — Author Profile](https://openbooks.net/authors/ama-owusu)\n- [Glassy-eyed — Cassava Press](https://openbooks.net/books/glassy-eyed)",
